  <title>2.9.7: Identifying Inequality Solutions on a Graph</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00513</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.9.7: Identifying Inequality Solutions on a Graph</md:title>
    <md:uuid>3d227313-f43c-4cd7-a6c3-0816a106184c</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
        <title>Student Activity</title>
     
        <para>Which graph correctly shows the solution to the inequality <span class="math math-repaired">\( \dfrac{7x-3}9 \geq 8-2x \)</span>? Show or explain your reasoning.</para>
        
          <para>A</para>
          <image alt="A number line is shown. There is an open circle on 3. The number line to the right of 3 is highlighted.&#10;" class="atto_image_button_text-bottom" height="22" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/2e5181154134c7cd7fc2b5f7dae48b8a06531e2a" width="361"/>
        
        
          <para>B</para>
          <image alt="A number line is shown. There is an open circle on 3. The number line to the left of 3 is highlighted." class="atto_image_button_text-bottom" height="22" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/3ea0124440695580d09e2ee8f6912aa1bc04e133" width="361"/>
        
        
          <para>C</para>
          <image alt="Alt Text: A number line is shown. There is a closed circle on 3. The number line to the right of 3 is highlighted.&#10;" class="atto_image_button_text-bottom" height="22" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/5f9cbe1e285f06fba5115a39c71b867bf673514b" width="361"/>
        
        
          <para>D</para>
          <image alt="A number line is shown. There is a closed circle on 3. The number line to the left of 3 is highlighted.&#10;" class="atto_image_button_text-bottom" height="22" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/804e2763d72ce690ee98333f42fa3d04c68773e4" width="361"/>
        
      
      <div class="summary">
        <para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis></para>
        <para>Your answers may vary, but here are some samples. Graph C.</para>
        <list>
          <item>I tested 2, 3, and 4 for the values of \(x\), and 3 and 4 make the inequality true.</item>
          <item>I solved a related equation and then tested a couple of values on either side of the solution.</item>
        </list>
        <title>Response to Student Thinking</title>
        <title>More Chances </title>
        <para>Students will have more opportunities to understand the mathematical ideas in this cool-down, so there is no need to slow down or add additional work to the next lessons. Instead, use the results of this cool-down to provide guidance for what to look for and emphasize over the next several lessons to support students in advancing their current understanding.</para>
        <para>A later activity offers another opportunity to discuss determining if a solution set is greater than or less than a boundary value.</para>
      

  
</div></section>
